uestion asks for):**\n- 8×GPU node, `P=4 × DP=2` and `P=8 × DP=1`, GPT-1.3B–7B mock data, bf16, `M=8P`, 30 steps, profiles on steps 10–15, 3 seeds, clocks pinned.\n- Instrument via `--use-pytorch-profiler` **and** nsys cross-check; per-rank busy = union of compute-kernel intervals within the step window (union, not sum, to avoid double-counting overlapped/async streams).\n- Define **operational bubble rate** = `1 − (1/P)·Σ_r busy_r / step_wall_time`, decomposed into: (i) structural idle, (ii) p2p comm wait, (iii) wgrad/optimizer-tail idle, (iv) allocator/recompute stalls, (v) launch-gap noise. Report per-rank and makespan-max variants.\n- Secondary ground-truth metric: **tokens/sec/GPU throughput and derived speedup vs. A0**, because zero *structural* bubble with +19% memory can still lose to 1F1B through recompute or comm — throughput is what falsifies \"practically near-zero\".\n\n**Decision rule:** claim supported only if Phase A structural bubble < 1% **and** Phase B operational bubble < 5% on the critical rank, with ≥1.1× throughput over 1F1B. Expected honest outcome (to be tested, not asserted): structural ≈ 0, operational materially > 0 — the ZB \"zero bubble\" is defined under uniform per-stage cost and ignored comm/wgrad tail, so the answer will likely be \"yes structurally, no in wall-clock practice\".\n\n**Uncertainties / consequential choices requiring researcher sign-off:** (a) exact flag spelling and whether `2P` or `2` is the correct value — must be read from source, not guessed; (b) whether a schedule-table dump is reachable on CPU without CUDA init (if not, Phase A needs a small test-harness shim, mirroring `tests/unit_tests/pipeline_parallel/`); (c) whether this repo is Megatron-LM, Megatron-Core, or NeMo, which changes both flag names and observability hooks; (d) whether GPU access can be provisioned at all — if not, the deliverable can only answer the structural half, and I should say so explicitly rather than imply a profiled result.", "evidence