{"id": "5ddb4589-7cf5-4b84-919c-f32f4b7058fa", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:11:09.198939", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "86dc6b89-76ef-4702-a9c4-c4666fed1dc2", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": "Confirmed again repo absent. Now write a small self-contained analytic simulator (self-authored, uniform-cost slot model) to validate:\n- bubble rate formula for 1F1B = (P-1)/M\n- VPP = (P-1)/(M*v)\n- show structural vs operational distinction.\n\nThis is a verification dry-run of my own metric definition, not a repo or ZB result. Let me write it.\n\nI'll implement:\n1. 1F1B schedule construction (standard), compute structural bubble = 1 - busy/(P*makespan) under uniform cost c, per-rank idle.\n2. Interleaved VPP.\n3. Optionally implement a ZB-H / ZB-2p-like schedule? That risks being misread as \"ZB-2p output\". I could implement the theoretical ZB-2p schedule from the paper's construction, but that would be my own reconstruction, not repo output. I think it's valuable to demonstrate the *upper bound* of what the design can do CPU-only: my own simulator could produce a ZB-H(2P) schedule and show structural bubble → 0, while operational (with comm cost) stays >0. But it must be labeled extremely clearly as \"designer-authored reference simulator, not the repo's scheduler; it exists to show the metric is non-degenerate and to sanity-check thresholds.\"\n\nHmm. Careful: researcher said don't fabricate. A self-authored simulator labeled clearly as such and not presented as the repo's ZB-2p is fine and is genuinely useful to show (a) analytic anchors hold in my slot model, (b) the metric discriminates. I'll do 1F1B + VPP anchors, and add a \"zero-bubble-form\" construction only if cheap... Actually implementing ZB-H correctly is nontrivial and a buggy version would be worse than nothing. I'll do a simpler, defensible demonstration: a \"zero-idle lower-bound\" idealized schedule (perfectly packed) to show the metric reads ~0 when there is truly no idle, plus adding a communication cost term to show operational bubble > 0. That's a metric non-degeneracy check, which is exactly what the negative control needs.\n\nLet me keep it tight: validate anchors (1F1B, VPP) and demonstrate a fully-packed schedule → structural 0 but operational > 0 once per-transfer comm cost is added. That's the crux of the design's decision rule.\n\nLet me write and run it.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "mkdir -p /workspace/design_checks && cat > /workspace/design_checks/metric_selfcheck.py <<'PY'\n\"\"\"\nMETRIC SELF-CHECK (design validation only).\n\nThis is a DESIGNER-AUTHORED analytic simulator. It is NOT the repository's\nscheduler and contains NO ZB/zero-bubble code (the repo is not mounted).\nIts only purpose is to verify that the Phase-A slot model and the\n\"bubble rate\" formula reproduce the *published analytic anchors* for\n1F1B and interleaved-VPP, and to show that the metric is non-degenerate\n(i.e. it can read ~0 structurally yet >0 operationally).\n\nUniform-cost slot model: every microbatch-forward = 1 slot, every\nmicrobatch-backward = 1 slot, per-stage layer counts equal.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef structural_bubble(P, busy_per_stage, makespan):\n    \"\"\"1 - total_busy / (P * makespan).\"\"\"\n    return 1.0 - sum(busy_per_stage) / float(P * makespan)\n\ndef one_f_one_b(P, M):\n    \"\"\"Per-stage busy/makespan for 1F1B (closed form).\"\"\"\n    makespan = M + 2 * (P - 1)          # warmup P-1 F, M steady, cooldown P-1 B\n    busy = [2 * M] * P                   # every stage does M fwd + M bwd\n    return makespan, busy\n\ndef vpp(P, M, v):\n    \"\"\"Interleaved 1F1B with v virtual chunks (closed form).\"\"\"\n    makespan = (M + 2 * (P - 1)) / float(v) + 0.0\n    busy = [2.0 * M] * P\n    return makespan, busy\n\nprint(\"anchor check: structural bubble vs published (P-1)/M and (P-1)/(M*v)\")\nprint(f\"{'P':>3} {'M':>4} {'1F1B sim':>10} {'1F1B exact':>11} {'VPP v=4 sim':>12} {'VPP exact':>10}\")\nfor P in (2, 4, 8):\n    for M in (8, 16, 32, 64):\n        mk, busy = one_f_one_b(P, M)\n        sim = structural_bubble(P, busy, mk)\n        exact = (P - 1) / float(M)\n        v = 4\n        mk2, busy2 = vpp(P, M, v)\n        sim2 = structural_bubble(P, busy2, mk2)\n        exact2 = (P - 1) / float(M * v)\n        ok = abs(sim - exact) < 1e-9 and abs(sim2 - exact2) < 1e-9\n        print(f\"{P:>3} {M:>4} {sim:>10.4f} {exact:>11.4f} {sim2:>12.4f} {exact2:>10.4f}   {'OK' if ok else 'MISMATCH'}\")\n\nprint()\nprint(\"non-degeneracy: a fully packed (structurally zero-idle) schedule\")\nprint(\"once a per-transfer comm cost c is charged on the critical path\")\nc_frac_of_microbatch = 0.05\nprint(f\"{'P':>3} {'M':>4} {'struct':>8} {'oper(c=%.2f slot/transfer)'%c_frac_of_microbatch:>30}\")\nfor P in (4, 8):\n    for M in (16, 32, 64):\n        # structurally packed: makespan == 2M busy slots per stage -> idle 0\n        struct = 0.0\n        # operational: 2*(P-1) p2p transfers on the critical path of each of\n        # M microbatches' fwd and bwd sweeps -> additive stall, not overlapped\n        work = 2.0 * M\n        stall = 2 * (P - 1) * c_frac_of_microbatch\n        oper = stall / (work + stall)\n        print(f\"{P:>3} {M:>4} {struct:>8.4f} {oper:>30.4f}\")\nPY\npython3 /workspace/design_checks/metric_selfcheck.py", "timeout_seconds": 60, "kind": "ExecuteCheckAction"}, "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-ae02483a2286f9a9", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-ae02483a2286f9a9", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "execute_check", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"mkdir -p /workspace/design_checks && cat > /workspace/design_checks/metric_selfcheck.py <<'PY'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nMETRIC SELF-CHECK (design validation only).\\n\\nThis is a DESIGNER-AUTHORED analytic simulator. It is NOT the repository's\\nscheduler and contains NO ZB/zero-bubble code (the repo is not mounted).\\nIts only purpose is to verify that the Phase-A slot model and the\\n\\\"bubble rat