{"id": "c8db742e-409b-462d-93fe-746d3e1ba50b", "timestamp": "2026-10-25T00:11:33.311792", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "02b67601-d867-4199-b026-d108f86babcf", "thought": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Anchor mismatch — my makespan formula was wrong. This is a real finding for the design (it exposes two different published \"bubble rate\" conventions). Let me correct and re-verify."}], "reasoning_content": "My makespan formula was wrong. Let me fix: 1F1B makespan in \"microbatch-computation units\" where one fwd+bwd pair = 2 units? Let's derive properly.\n\nUnit: 1 slot = one microbatch forward = 1 slot; one microbatch backward = 1 slot. Stage does M forwards + M backwards = 2M busy slots.\n\n1F1B makespan: warmup P-1 forwards, then M steady-state 1F1B pairs, then P-1 cooldown backwards. Total per stage = (P-1) + M*2 + (P-1) = 2M + 2(P-1). And in 1F1B each stage is busy the entire time after its start (approximately), so makespan ≈ 2M + 2(P-1) plus startup offsets. Actually stage 0 starts at t=0 and stage s starts at t=s. The makespan is max over stages of (start_s + busy) = for stage 0: 0 + 2M + 2(P-1) = 2M+2P-2. Hmm, standard result: 1F1B total time ≈ (M + P - 1) * (t_f + t_b) = (M+P-1)*2 in our units. That's 2M + 2P - 2. Same thing. Good.\n\nSo makespan = 2M + 2(P-1), busy per stage = 2M. Bubble = 1 - 2M/(2M+2(P-1)) = (P-1)/(M+P-1). Hmm, that's not (P-1)/M.\n\nThe classic bubble fraction formula is bubble/(bubble+work) = (P-1)/M ... let's check: ideal time = M*(t_f+t_b) per stage = 2M. Actual = 2(M+P-1). Overhead ratio = (P-1)/M measured against ideal work: (actual - ideal)/ideal = (P-1)/M. Yes! The published (P-1)/M is overhead relative to *useful work*, not relative to wall-clock. Whereas my formula 1 - busy/makespan gives (P-1)/(M+P-1), which is idle fraction of wall-clock.\n\nThis is a genuinely important distinction for the design — the two conventions differ, and \"near-zero bubble rate\" thresholds depend on which. Great, this is exactly the kind of thing to surface. Let me rewrite the check to compute BOTH conventions and verify:\n- convention A (wall-clock idle fraction): (P-1)/(M+P-1)\n- convention B (overhead vs. ideal work, the \"bubble ratio\" in many PP papers): (P-1)/M\n\nAnd VPP: makespan = 2(M + (P-1)/v) → wall-clock idle = (P-1)/((P-1)+Mv), overhead-vs-work = (P-1)/(Mv).\n\nLet me redo the script correctly. Also makespan for VPP in our units: 2*(M + (P-1)/v).\n\nLet me rewrite.\n", "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"command": "cat > /workspace/design_checks/metric_selfcheck.py <<'PY'\n\"\"\"\nMETRIC SELF-CHECK (design validation only -- NOT an experiment, NOT repo code).\n\nDesigner-authored analytic model. The repository is NOT mounted, so no\nZB / zero-bubble schedule is evaluated here. Purpose:\n  (1) verify the Phase-A slot model reproduces the published PP anchors;\n  (2) discover WHICH closed form the anchors correspond to, because two\n      different \"bubble rate\" conventions are in circulation and they\n      differ materially -> the design must name one.\nUniform-cost slot model: 1 slot = one microbatch forward (or one backward);\nequal layers per stage.\n\"\"\"\n\ndef conventions(P, busy_per_stage, makespan):\n    \"\"\"Return (wall-clock idle fraction, overhead-vs-ideal-work ratio).\"\"\"\n    total_capacity = P * makespan\n    total_busy = sum(busy_per_stage)\n    idle_frac = 1.0 - total_busy / float(total_capacity)   # idle / wall-clock\n    ideal = busy_per_stage[0]                              # no-PP per-stage work\n    overhead = (makespan - ideal) / float(ideal)           # (actual-ideal)/ideal\n    return idle_frac, overhead\n\nprint(\"convention check (busy per stage = 2M; makespan = 2(M+P-1) for 1F1B)\")\nprint(f\"{'P':>3} {'M':>4} | {'A:idle/wall':>11} {'(P-1)/(M+P-1)':>15} | \"\n      f\"{'B:over/ideal':>12} {'(P-1)/M':>8}\")\nbad = 0\nfor P in (2, 4, 8):\n    for M in (8, 16, 32, 64):\n        busy = [2 * M] * P\n        mk =